        <li><b>Cache</b> if you replace a file with the same name (favicon, og.jpg), bump its version in the address (<code>?v=NN</code>): social networks and browsers keep the old one.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3 class="font-display text-h3 sub">A new project in the portfolio</h3>
      <p class="cuerpo">You add an entry to <code>src/data/proyectos.ts</code> and its media to <code>public/media/obra/&lt;slug&gt;/</code>. The case page and its place in /proyectos come out by themselves. The fields:</p>
      <dl class="dev-filas">{CAMPOS_EN.map(([t, d]) => (<div><dt><code>{t}</code></dt><dd>{d}</dd></div>))}</dl>
      <ul class="reglas">
        <li><b>Only facts</b> the copy of the case comes from what is on record (the project, its website, its documents). Nothing made up.</li>
        <li><b>Permission</b> before showing the website, the logo or the quote of a client.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="secciones" class="seccion" aria-labelledby="h-secciones">
      <h2 id="h-secciones" class="font-display text-h2">Adding a section</h2>
      <p class="cuerpo">Each section of the home page is a component in <code>src/components/</code> placed, in its order, in <code>src/pages/index.astro</code>. Today: Hero, Raices, Dolores, Proyectos, Anteriores, Servicios, LaPartitura, Estudio, Preguntas, and the Pie outside main.</p>
      <ol class="pasos">
        <li>
          <h3 class="font-display text-h3">The component</h3>
          <p>A <code>&lt;section&gt;</code> with its id (it is the anchor: <code>/#servicios</code>), the <code>wrap</code> container and the section spacing <code>section-y</code>. The copy, in <code>home.ts</code>; the styles, scoped inside the component.</p>
          <pre><code>&lt;section id="nueva" class="surface-light"&gt;
  &lt;div class="wrap section-y"&gt;
    &lt;h2 class="font-display text-h2" data-entra&gt;…&lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;p class="text-sub text-fg2" data-enfoca&gt;…&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="font-display text-h3">Tokens, never loose values</h3>
          <p>Surface <code>surface-dark</code>, <code>surface-light</code> or <code>surface-warm</code> (Services); text <code>text-fg</code> and <code>text-fg2</code>, rules <code>border-rule</code>; sizes <code>text-h1, h2, h3, lead, sub, body, ui, detail</code>; spacing only in the steps of the guide. The colours change by themselves with the season.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="font-display text-h3">The entrance</h3>
          <p><code>src/scripts/entradas.ts</code> gives three movements by attribute: <code>data-entra</code> on headlines (the words rise from a mask), <code>data-enfoca</code> on blocks (from blurred to sharp) and <code>data-sube</code> on every section that CHANGES COLOUR from the previous one (the liquid drop that arrives through the centre).</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="font-display text-h3">The rails</h3>
          <p><code>Carriles.astro</code> draws a line with two crosses at the start of each section in main. <code>data-sin-fila</code> on the section removes it; <code>data-carril-fila</code> on an element adds another (with <code>="sin-cruces"</code>, just the line).</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="font-display text-h3">No repeats</h3>
          <p>A section does not copy the skeleton of another, and it is not an effect for the sake of the effect: AGENTS.md › “Rejected” says so with examples.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

