      <h2 id="h-paginas" class="font-display text-h2">Adding a page</h2>
      <p class="cuerpo">A page is a file in <code>src/pages/</code>: its route is its name (<code>lab.astro</code> → /lab; <code>proyectos/[slug].astro</code> → one case per project). They all share the same skeleton.</p>
      <pre><code>---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Carriles from '../components/Carriles.astro';
import Pie from '../components/Pie.astro';
---
&lt;Base title="A new savvia page" description="One sentence." carga=&#123;false&#125;&gt;
  &lt;Nav /&gt;
  &lt;Carriles /&gt;
  &lt;main id="contenido" class="surface-light"&gt;…&lt;/main&gt;
  &lt;Pie /&gt;
&lt;/Base&gt;</code></pre>
      <dl class="dev-filas">
        <div><dt><code>Base.astro</code></dt><dd>Three options: <code>title</code>, <code>description</code> and <code>carga</code> (the loading animation; set it to <code>false</code>: only the home page has it). It sets the season, the fonts, the favicon, the share image and the noindex.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Nav, Carriles, Pie</dt><dd>The bar with the menu, the guides along the edges and the footer with the landscape. The Lab has no Carriles: its canvas is endless.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Light or dark</dt><dd>Secondary pages are light (<code>surface-light</code>), a decision from round 128.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>The menu</dt><dd>For it to appear there, add it to <code>nav.links</code> or to <code>nav.mas</code> in <code>home.ts</code>.</dd></div>
