      </dl>
      <h3 class="font-display text-h3 sub">Guardrails: what is not accepted</h3>
      <dl class="dev-filas">{GUARDARRAILES_EN.map(([t, d]) => (<div><dt><code>{t}</code></dt><dd>{d}</dd></div>))}</dl>
    </section>

    <section id="pedir" class="seccion" aria-labelledby="h-pedir">
      <h2 id="h-pedir" class="font-display text-h2">Asking for changes</h2>
      <p class="cuerpo">A few rules help Claude get it right the first time and keep the website tidy.</p>
      <dl class="dev-filas">
        <div><dt>What, where and how it ends up</dt><dd>“Change X to Y in the hero” works better than “improve the hero”.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>One thing, or a numbered list</dt><dd>If there are several, number them: each one is done, measured and noted separately.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>In your own words</dt><dd>What you ask for is copied as it is into the log. There is no need to polish it.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Point at it</dt><dd>A screenshot, or an Agentation note pinned to the element locally: that way there is no doubt about which piece it is.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Name things with this system</dt><dd>“The accent of the season”, “the glass CTA”, “the ‹ 01/04 › bar”, “the drop between sections”.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Say what not to touch</dt><dd>“Without moving the tree”, “only on mobile”, “the rest stays as it is”.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>What was rejected does not come back</dt><dd>If you ask for something listed under “Rejected” in AGENTS.md, Claude will tell you. If it really needs to come back, the two of you decide and it is noted.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tests that can be undone</dt><dd>To try something you are unsure about, ask for it to sit behind a parameter (<code>?bloque=hielo</code>, <code>?carga=1</code>) without touching the rest.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <h3 class="font-display text-h3 sub">Well made requests</h3>
      <ul class="peticiones">
        <li>“In the hero, the subtitle becomes: ‘Specialists in orchestrating agentic development.’. The headline stays as it is.”</li>
        <li>“In More projects: 1. the client name moves down to the foot of the card; 2. more space between rows; 3. the last row, only two projects.”</li>
        <li>“The hero roots in winter have a halftone that the canopy does not have. Remove it from the roots only.” (with a screenshot)</li>
        <li>“Add the [client] project to the portfolio: here is the website and the copy for the case. It should not appear among the featured ones.”</li>
        <li>“I want to try the winter blue in Services, but as a test that is easy to remove.”</li>
        <li>“The × in the seated view sometimes opens the menu: it should never happen. Test it on mobile too.”</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </Fragment>
)}

