      <div><dt>WebGL contexts</dt><dd>The oak, the roots, the footer landscape and the Manifesto are painted by the engine <code>src/scripts/estela.ts</code>, one WebGL canvas each. Chrome and Safari keep about 16 at a time and drop the oldest (in round 63 the hero went blank). That is why estela.ts PUTS TO SLEEP the distant canvases when more than <code>LIMITE</code> are alive (12 in Chrome; in Safari, always) and wakes them up as you get close. Before adding another canvas, count them.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Fonts</dt><dd>Self-hosted with Astro’s font API (<code>astro.config.mjs</code>, files in <code>src/assets/fonts/</code>). Family is the TRIAL file from Klim: no accents or ñ (they fall back to Georgia) and it cannot be served openly without a licence: it has to be bought. Timeless (Sans, Grotesk) comes with the Timeless Free Font License 1.2 (<code>tools/fuentes-timeless/</code>): free for web and commercial use, but redistributing it or uploading it to a public repository is forbidden. Ours is private and must stay that way.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>noindex</dt><dd>Everything is indexed. A page that should stay out of search engines passes <code>indexar</code> as <code>false</code> to <code>Base.astro</code>, like the Method and the 404. The sitemap comes from <code>@astrojs/sitemap</code>.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Sounds</dt><dd>The printer, the ambiences and the music of the reel come from Pixabay (free to use without attribution); the source, author and excerpt of each one are in <code>tools/fuentes-sonido.md</code>. The radio, from HoliznaCC0 (public domain), matched to −18 LUFS. Nothing marked “all rights reserved”.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Backups</dt><dd>What is removed is not deleted: it goes to <code>tools/retirados/</code> with the round in its name. Andoni also keeps a copy of the folder before each large round (<code>../savvia-web.bak-rNN-fecha/</code>, on his Mac). And Git keeps every commit.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>If Vercel blocks a deployment</dt><dd>It happens when the commit comes from someone who is not in Andoni’s Vercel team: it stays as “Deployment was blocked” (round 83). Since round 174 the <code>publicar.yml</code> Action calls the Deploy Hook (the repository secret <code>VERCEL_DEPLOY_HOOK</code>) and publishes it anyway. If it still does not go out: Andoni hits Redeploy in Vercel or pushes a commit of his own (an empty one will do). So it does not happen again, each person sets up their Git identity with their GitHub email.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>In an emergency</dt><dd>The old recipe still works: <code>astro build</code> and <code>vercel deploy --prod</code> from <code>dist/</code>, with the <code>savvia-home</code> project.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>
)}

